Keeps the LMS positions of libsais_main_8u's first pass as a bitmap
where 0001-keep-lms-positions.patch cannot keep them as a list, instead
of finding them again. Applies after 0003-repetitive-recursion.patch.

Patch 0001 keeps the list of m LMS positions in the last m ints of the
free space where fs >= m and fs + n >= 4m. The work array gives
fs >= n/2, so that holds up to m/n = 3/8, and not on the full blocks of
inputs above it (MC:Z, about 0.40). There this patch keeps a bitmap of
the positions instead, one bit per position of T in whole machine words
(bzng_lms_bitmap_ints, b = about n/32 ints), in the last b ints of the
free space, built from the first pass's list before the radix sort
overwrites that. After the recursion it writes the positions back,
ascending, to SA[n - m..n), where libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u would
have put them, and the reconstruction is libsais's as before; the suffix
array is the same.

It does so where fs >= b + 4, which puts the bitmap beyond SA[0..n + 4)
(writing the positions back stores up to 4 entries past SA[n - 1], into
free space the recursion has finished with), and fs - b + n >= 3m, which
leaves the recursion fs - b + n - 2m >= m ints of free space, at least
its length, so the argument of docs/spec.md section 4.3 still rules out
an allocation. With fs = n/2 that is every block up to m/n of about 0.49
(0.4896 at n = 900,000; no block reaches 0.5). Elsewhere the positions
are found again as before. The functions are bz2-ng's, in
lib/sort_libsais.c, which defines them before it includes this file.

Measured on the M4 with Apple clang 21 and gcc 16, bz2-ng's encoder at
level 9 unless stated, 5 rounds interleaved with an identical-binary
control, every build with -falign-functions=64, against the same tree
without this patch: MC:Z whole file 1.051 (clang) and 1.048 (gcc), at
level 1 1.050 and 1.049; Silesia's x-ray 1.022 and 1.022, at level 1
1.022 and 1.021; faster in every round. Silesia's mr 1.011 and 1.017, at
level 1 1.016 and 1.013, half of whose blocks lie above the bitmap's
edge. Even: MC:Z in 16 KiB, 64 KiB and 640 kB streams (their blocks
keep the list, the level-9 work array being sized for 900 kB blocks),
XA:Z and quality strings in every stream size, and Silesia. Timed alone
on 900 kB of MC:Z, building the bitmap and writing the positions back
take 0.16 ms/MB, the second pass over T 0.72 ms/MB. The decoder's code
is unchanged.

On the three Linux reference machines, the same method, each box pinned
to one CPU, MC:Z whole file at level 9 with gcc 13 and clang 18: Zen 5
1.037 and 1.029, Granite Rapids 1.031 and 1.032, Graviton4 1.047 and
1.043. Every other compression cell even but one, quality strings in
16 KiB streams with clang on Granite Rapids at 0.976, whose blocks keep
the list: code placement.

--- a/libsais.c
+++ b/libsais.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * 0001-keep-lms-positions.patch
  * 0002-bwt-row.patch
  * 0003-repetitive-recursion.patch
+ * 0004-keep-lms-bitmap.patch
  */
 
 /*--
@@ -6990,6 +6991,18 @@
          */
         sa_sint_t keep_lms_suffixes = fs >= m && (fs + n) / 4 >= m;
         if (keep_lms_suffixes) { fs -= m; memcpy(&SA[n + fs], &SA[n - m], (size_t)m * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
+
+        /*
+         * Where the list does not fit, a bitmap of the positions, b ints
+         * from bzng_lms_bitmap_ints (lib/sort_libsais.c, included before
+         * this file), is kept the same way: fs >= b + 4 puts it beyond
+         * SA[0..n + 4), which writing the positions back may overrun by
+         * 4 entries, and fs - b + n >= 3m leaves the recursion
+         * fs - b + n - 2m >= m ints of free space, at least its length.
+         */
+        sa_sint_t lms_bitmap_ints = bzng_lms_bitmap_ints(n);
+        sa_sint_t keep_lms_bitmap = !keep_lms_suffixes && fs - 4 >= lms_bitmap_ints && (fs - lms_bitmap_ints + n) / 3 >= m;
+        if (keep_lms_bitmap) { fs -= lms_bitmap_ints; bzng_lms_bitmap_store(&SA[n - m], m, &SA[n + fs], lms_bitmap_ints); }
 
         if (threads > 1 && n >= 65536) { memset(SA, 0, ((size_t)n - (size_t)m) * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
         libsais_radix_sort_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, m, flags, buckets, threads, thread_state);
@@ -7017,6 +7030,11 @@
             if (keep_lms_suffixes)
             {
                 libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n + fs + m, m, threads);
+            }
+            else if (keep_lms_bitmap)
+            {
+                bzng_lms_bitmap_load(&SA[n + fs], lms_bitmap_ints, &SA[n - m]);
+                libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n, m, threads);
             }
             else
